     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r4",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "58. The duty of service is most difficult to be understood;",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "it is beyond the ken of even sages: (for a servant is called ),",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "dumb if he is silent ! ( if he is ) ready with his answer, he is",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "talkative or garrulous; if he stands near, he is impudent; and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "then if he keeps at a distance, he is timid; if he bears pa-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "tiently, he is a coward; if he cannot brook ( harsh words, in-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "sults &c. ) he is generally considered mannerless.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r5",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "59. Who can live happily when within the range of a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "wicked man who hates merit, who has by chance attained",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "greatness, and has forgotten his former mode of obtaining a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "living by base deeds, and who, free from all restraint, has",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "whitewashed all other wicked people.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r6",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "60. The friendship of wicked men and of good men",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "differs like the shadow in the first and the second half of the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "day (respectively)—extensive at the beginning, but gradual-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "ly contracting ( in the first part while in the latter ) at first",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "scant, but attaining growth afterwards.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r7",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "61. The deer, the fish, and the virtuous, living on grass,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "water and contentment respectively ( find ) in this world un-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "provoked enemies ( in ) the hunter, the fisherman, and the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "wicked.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  {
   "id": "r8",
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "62. A bow to those men in whom reside the following",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "sterling qualities:—desire for the company of the virtuous,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "satisfaction at the merits of others, humility towards elders,",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "attachment to learning, love for one’s own wife, fear of",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
